In *my* experience, contact lenses.  (My sister is very good at this, which is
another reason why I decided to stick with glasses....)

Anyway, I raise that point becuase it has some interesting ideas hidden in it.
How about adding some form of contact lenses to a game?  They would be handled
like rings, and would alter your intrinsics while you're wearing them:  the
usual kind would improve distance vision (unless cursed), with higher +'s
giving better distance vision (but correspondingly reducing *close* vision
unless removed or blessed).  Cursed lenses, of course, would reduce your
vision.  Other, less common kinds of lenses would confer various kinds of
clairvoyance (detect monsters or treasure, see through walls for a short
distance, detect magic, see invisible...), with corresponding effects for
blessed/cursed lenses.  (A cursed "see invisible" contact lens would cause
blindness, for example, while a cursed "detect monsters" would make all
monsters invisible.)

